@* The SHARED account-statement screen - the biggest control in this module (896 lines of
   procedural WebForms).

   ⚠ WHY THIS COMPONENT EXISTS - A SHARED CODE-BEHIND IN THE ORIGINAL.
   Reports/AccountStatement.ascx AND Reports/AccountStatementPopup.ascx both declared
       CodeBehind="AccountStatement.ascx.cs"
       Inherits="MixERP.Net.Core.Modules.Finance.Reports.AccountStatement"
   i.e. ONE class served BOTH .ascx files (the popup had no .cs and no .designer.cs of its
   own). Treating the popup as "a control with no code-behind" would have silently emptied the
   screen the balance sheet's drill-down opens. The sharing is preserved STRUCTURALLY here so
   the two cannot drift: this component carries the whole screen, and
   Reports/AccountStatement.razor + Reports/AccountStatementPopup.razor are thin hosts that
   differ only in what the two .ascx files differed in (the popup's MasterPageId and its
   padding wrapper).

   It is a plain component, not a MixERPUserControl: the two HOSTS are the user controls (they
   carry the authorization run and the probe-visible flags). It therefore injects ICurrentLogin
   itself.

   THE MARKUP IS THE CONTROL TREE, in the identical child order the eight builders produced:
     h2                                              CreateHeader()
     div.ui.icon.buttons.bpad16                      CreateTopPanel()
       > button#AddNewButton / #FlagButton / #ReconcileButton / #PrintButton
       > input#SelectedValuesHidden                  AddHiddenFields()
     div.ui.top.attached.tabular.menu > two <a data-tab>   CreateTabs()
     div.ui.bottom.attached.active.form.tab.segment[data-tab=first]
       > div.fields  (account number, select, from, to, Show)   CreateFormPanel()
       > div.auto-overflow-panel > table#StatementGridView      CreateGridPanel()
     div.ui.bottom.attached.tab.segment[data-tab=second]        the account overview tab
     <Flag>                                          CreateFlagPanel()
     div#ReconcileModal.ui.small.modal               CreateReconcileModal()

   ⚠ #StatementGridView IS A POSITIONAL JAVASCRIPT CONTRACT. js/reports/AccountStatement.js
   declares checkBoxColumnPosition = "2", tranCodeColumnPosition = "3" and
   bookDateColumnPosition = "5", the print-icon handler reads td:nth-child(3), and
   createFlaggedRows() reads the two trailing flag colour columns. So all FIFTEEN columns are
   emitted in the original order - the print-icon template, the select-checkbox template, then
   the 13 bound fields ending with FlagBg and FlagFg, whose headers are deliberately EMPTY.
   The two templates render exactly what the ITemplate/GridViewSelectTemplate produced:
   `<i class="icon print" onclick="showPreview(this);"></i>` and
   `<div class="ui toggle checkbox"><input type="checkbox" /><label></label></div>`.
   "{0:d}" and "{0:N}" are applied by GridFormat, reproducing BoundField.DataFormatString
   (current culture, and a null cell rendered empty).

   THE SHOW BUTTON AND THE FLAG ARE SERVER HANDLERS and stay so:
     * ShowButton_Click -> BindGridView() + CreateAccountOverviewPanel(), i.e. it refreshes
       BOTH tabs - preserved;
     * Flag_Updated -> Flags.CreateFlag(...) over the SELECTED transaction codes, then the same
       two refreshes. Its resource/resourceKey constants ("account_statement",
       "transaction_code") and the comma-split of #SelectedValuesHidden are verbatim; that
       hidden field is filled by the script's getSelectedItems(), which also gates the flag
       popup through OnClientClick - so it is read at click time through ElementValueReader
       (the WebForms postback read of a jQuery-written field has no other equivalent).
     * the date boxes are read the same way, because the jQuery UI datepicker writes them
       without raising an input event.

   AutoInitialize() is preserved verbatim, including its own quirk: it reads ?AccountNumber= or
   resolves ?AccountId= through AccountHelper, applies ?From= / ?To= only when they are not
   DateTime.MinValue, and RETURNS EARLY - binding nothing - when neither an account number nor
   an account id was supplied. That is why the grid is empty until Show is pressed on the
   normal screen, and pre-filled when the balance sheet opens the popup with ?AccountId=&To=.

   ⚠ PRE-EXISTING BUG, PRESERVED: GetDateField() built a calendar icon
   (`<i class="icon calendar pointer" onclick="$('#...').datepicker('show');">`) inside a
   `using` block and NEVER ADDED IT, so that icon has never rendered. It is deliberately not
   emitted - adding it would newly switch on a click handler the screen never had. The
   "ui icon input" wrapper it would have lived in IS emitted, because that one was added.

   StatementGridViewDataBound (HeaderRow.TableSection) is dropped with no loss - a real
   <thead> is emitted. *@

@using System.Collections.ObjectModel
@using System.Data
@using MixERP.Net.Common
@using MixERP.Net.Core.Modules.Finance.Data.Helpers
@using MixERP.Net.Entities
@using MixERP.Net.Entities.Core
@using MixERP.Net.Entities.Transactions
@using MixERP.Net.Framework.Security
@using MixERP.Net.TransactionGovernor
@using MixERP.Net.WebControls.Common
@using MixERP.Net.WebControls.Flag
@using MixERP.Net.i18n.Resources
@inject ICurrentLogin CurrentLogin
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IJSRuntime JS

@* CreateHeader() *@
<h2>@Titles.AccountStatement</h2>

@* CreateTopPanel() *@
<div class="ui icon buttons bpad16">
    <button id="AddNewButton" class="ui button"
            onclick="window.location='/Modules/Finance/Entry/JournalVoucher.mix';return false;">
        <i class='icon plus'></i>@Titles.NewJournalEntry
    </button>
    <button id="FlagButton" class="ui button" onclick="return false;">
        <i class='icon flag'></i>@Titles.Flag
    </button>
    <button id="ReconcileButton" class="ui button" onclick="return showReconcileWindow();">
        <i class='circle notched icon'></i>@Titles.Reconcile
    </button>
    <button id="PrintButton" class="ui button" onclick="return false;">
        <i class='icon print'></i>@Titles.Print
    </button>
    <input type="hidden" id="SelectedValuesHidden" />
</div>

@* CreateTabs() - the tab menu *@
<div class="ui top attached tabular menu">
    <a class="active item" data-tab="first">@Titles.TransactionStatement</a>
    <a class="item" data-tab="second">@Titles.AccountOverview</a>
</div>

@* CreateTabs() - the first tab: the form panel and the grid panel *@
<div class="ui bottom attached active form tab segment" data-tab="first">
    <div class="fields">
        <div class="field">
            <label for="AccountNumberInputText">@Titles.AccountNumber</label>
            <input type="text" id="AccountNumberInputText" value="@this.accountNumber" />
        </div>
        <div class="four wide field">
            <label for="AccountNumberSelect">@Titles.Select</label>
            <select id="AccountNumberSelect"></select>
        </div>
        @* GetDateField(Titles.From, fromDateTextBox) - see the calendar-icon note above. *@
        <div class="field">
            <label for="FromDateTextBox">@Titles.From</label>
            <div class="ui icon input">
                <DateTextBox ID="FromDateTextBox" Mode="@(FrequencyType.FiscalYearStartDate)"
                             Catalog="@this.catalog" OfficeId="@this.officeId" @bind-Text="this.fromDate" />
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
            <label for="ToDateTextBox">@Titles.To</label>
            <div class="ui icon input">
                <DateTextBox ID="ToDateTextBox" Mode="@(FrequencyType.FiscalYearEndDate)"
                             Catalog="@this.catalog" OfficeId="@this.officeId" @bind-Text="this.toDate" />
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
            <label for="ShowButton">@Titles.Prepare</label>
            <button id="ShowButton" type="button" class="ui positive button"
                    @onclick="this.ShowButton_Click">@Titles.Show</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="auto-overflow-panel">
        <table id="StatementGridView" class="ui celled table nowrap">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th></th>
                    <th>@Titles.Select</th>
                    <th>@Titles.TranCode</th>
                    <th>@Titles.ValueDate</th>
                    <th>@Titles.BookDate</th>
                    <th class="text right">@Titles.Debit</th>
                    <th class="text right">@Titles.Credit</th>
                    <th class="text right">@Titles.Balance</th>
                    <th>@Titles.StatementReference</th>
                    <th>@Titles.Office</th>
                    <th>@Titles.Book</th>
                    <th>@Titles.AccountNumber</th>
                    <th>@Titles.Account</th>
                    <th></th>
                    <th></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @if (this.statement != null)
                {
                    @foreach (DbGetAccountStatementResult row in this.statement)
                    {
                        <tr>
                            @* ActionTemplate *@
                            <td><i class="icon print" onclick="showPreview(this);"></i></td>
                            @* GridViewHelper.GridViewSelectTemplate *@
                            <td>
                                <div class="ui toggle checkbox"><input type="checkbox" /><label></label></div>
                            </td>
                            <td>@row.TranCode</td>
                            <td>@GridFormat.Format(row.ValueDate, "{0:d}")</td>
                            <td>@GridFormat.Format(row.BookDate, "{0:d}")</td>
                            <td class="text right">@GridFormat.Format(row.Debit, "{0:N}")</td>
                            <td class="text right">@GridFormat.Format(row.Credit, "{0:N}")</td>
                            <td class="text right">@GridFormat.Format(row.Balance, "{0:N}")</td>
                            <td>@row.StatementReference</td>
                            <td>@row.Office</td>
                            <td>@row.Book</td>
                            <td>@row.AccountNumber</td>
                            <td>@row.Account</td>
                            <td>@row.FlagBg</td>
                            <td>@row.FlagFg</td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

@* CreateTabs() - the second tab, filled by CreateAccountOverviewPanel() *@
<div class="ui bottom attached tab segment" data-tab="second">
    @if (this.overview != null)
    {
        @* CreateAccountOverviewHeader(): an h2 carrying a Literal, then a .description div
           carrying a Literal. The description literal was NEVER assigned by the original, so
           it rendered empty - preserved. *@
        <h2>@this.overview.Account</h2>
        <div class="description"></div>

        @* CreateAccountOverviewTable() *@
        <table id="AccountOverViewGrid" class="ui definition table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th></th>
                    <th>@Titles.Definition</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Titles.AccountNumber</td>
                    <td>@this.overview.AccountNumber</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Titles.ExternalCode</td>
                    <td>@this.overview.ExternalCode</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Titles.BaseCurrency</td>
                    <td>@this.overview.CurrencyCode</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Titles.AccountMaster</td>
                    <td>@this.overview.AccountMasterCode</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Titles.Confidential</td>
                    <td>@Conversion.TryCastString(this.overview.Confidential)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Titles.IsSystemAccount</td>
                    <td>@Conversion.TryCastString(this.overview.SysType)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Titles.NormallyDebit</td>
                    <td>@Conversion.TryCastString(this.overview.NormallyDebit)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>@Titles.ParentAccount</td>
                    <td>@this.overview.ParentAccountNumber</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    }
</div>

@* CreateFlagPanel() *@
@if (this.catalog != null)
{
    <Flag ElementId="FlagPopUnder"
          AssociatedControlId="FlagButton"
          OnClientClick="return getSelectedItems();"
          CssClass="ui form segment initially hidden"
          Catalog="@this.catalog"
          Updated="@this.Flag_Updated" />
}

@* CreateReconcileModal() - every button is script-driven (reconcile() / modal("hide")), so the
   onclick values are carried over as HTML attributes, as the originals were. *@
<div id="ReconcileModal" class="ui small modal">
    @((MarkupString)MixERP.Net.Common.Helpers.HtmlControlHelper.GetIcon("close icon"))
    @((MarkupString)MixERP.Net.Common.Helpers.HtmlControlHelper.GetModalHeader(Titles.Reconcile, "circle notched icon"))
    <div class="content">
        <div class="ui form">
            <div class="two fields">
                <div class="field">
                    <label for="TranCodeInputText">@Titles.TranCode</label>
                    <input type="text" id="TranCodeInputText" disabled="disabled" />
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label for="CurrentBookDateInputText">@Titles.CurrentBookDate</label>
                    <input type="text" id="CurrentBookDateInputText" disabled="disabled" />
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="field">
                <label>@Titles.NewBookDate</label>
                <div class="three fields">
                    <div class="field">
                        <input type="text" id="YearInputText" placeholder="@Titles.Year" class="integer" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="field">
                        <input type="text" id="MonthInputText" placeholder="@Titles.Month" class="integer" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="field">
                        <input type="text" id="DayInputText" placeholder="@Titles.Day" class="integer" />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <input type="button" class="ui green button" value="@Titles.OK" onclick="reconcile();" />
            <input type="button" class="ui red button" value="@Titles.Close"
                   onclick="$(&quot;#ReconcileModal&quot;).modal(&quot;hide&quot;);" />
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private const string Resource = "account_statement";
    private const string ResourceKey = "transaction_code";

    private ElementValueReader elementValues;

    private string catalog;
    private int userId;
    private int officeId;

    private string accountNumber;
    private string fromDate;
    private string toDate;

    private IEnumerable<DbGetAccountStatementResult> statement;
    private AccountView overview;

    /// <summary>
    ///     True once the screen has rendered its data at least once; the host component uses it
    ///     to decide when the controller script may be loaded (it reads the rendered rows).
    /// </summary>
    public bool Ready { get; private set; }

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        await base.OnInitializedAsync();

        this.elementValues = new ElementValueReader(this.JS);

        LoginInfo login = await this.CurrentLogin.GetLoginAsync();

        this.userId = login.UserId;
        this.officeId = login.OfficeId;
        this.catalog = await this.CurrentLogin.GetCatalogAsync();

        this.AutoInitialize();

        this.Ready = true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Port of AutoInitialize(), verbatim - including the EARLY RETURN when neither an
    ///     account number nor a resolvable account id was supplied, which is what leaves the
    ///     grid and the overview tab empty on a cold open.
    /// </summary>
    private void AutoInitialize()
    {
        string queryAccountNumber = ModuleQuery.Get(this.Navigation, "AccountNumber");
        long accountId = Conversion.TryCastLong(ModuleQuery.Get(this.Navigation, "AccountId"));
        DateTime from = Conversion.TryCastDate(ModuleQuery.Get(this.Navigation, "From"));
        DateTime to = Conversion.TryCastDate(ModuleQuery.Get(this.Navigation, "To"));

        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(queryAccountNumber))
        {
            this.accountNumber = queryAccountNumber;
        }
        else
        {
            if (accountId > 0)
            {
                this.accountNumber = AccountHelper.GetAccountNumberByAccountId(this.catalog, accountId);
            }
            else
            {
                return;
            }
        }

        if (from != DateTime.MinValue)
        {
            this.fromDate = from.Date.ToShortDateString();
        }

        if (to != DateTime.MinValue)
        {
            this.toDate = to.Date.ToShortDateString();
        }

        this.BindGridView();
        this.CreateAccountOverviewPanel();
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Port of ShowButton_Click: BOTH the grid and the overview tab are rebuilt. The three
    ///     filter values are re-read from the DOM first, which is what the postback did.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ShowButton_Click()
    {
        await this.ReadFiltersAsync();

        this.BindGridView();
        this.CreateAccountOverviewPanel();
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Port of Flag_Updated, verbatim: the flag is recorded against the SELECTED
    ///     transaction codes and both panels are then rebuilt.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task Flag_Updated(FlagUpdatedEventArgs e)
    {
        if (e == null)
        {
            return;
        }

        int flagTypeId = e.FlagId;

        Collection<string> selected = await this.GetSelectedValuesAsync();

        Flags.CreateFlag(this.catalog, this.userId, flagTypeId, Resource, ResourceKey, selected);

        await this.ReadFiltersAsync();

        this.BindGridView();
        this.CreateAccountOverviewPanel();
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Port of GetSelectedValues(): the comma-separated transaction codes the script's
    ///     getSelectedItems() wrote into #SelectedValuesHidden. Blank means an empty
    ///     collection, exactly as before.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task<Collection<string>> GetSelectedValuesAsync()
    {
        string selectedValues = await this.elementValues.GetValueAsync("SelectedValuesHidden");

        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(selectedValues))
        {
            return new Collection<string>();
        }

        Collection<string> values = new Collection<string>();

        foreach (string value in selectedValues.Split(','))
        {
            values.Add(value);
        }

        return values;
    }

    private async Task ReadFiltersAsync()
    {
        string account = await this.elementValues.GetValueAsync("AccountNumberInputText");
        string from = await this.elementValues.GetValueAsync("FromDateTextBox");
        string to = await this.elementValues.GetValueAsync("ToDateTextBox");

        if (account != null)
        {
            this.accountNumber = account;
        }

        if (from != null)
        {
            this.fromDate = from;
        }

        if (to != null)
        {
            this.toDate = to;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Port of BindGridView(), verbatim - the same six arguments in the same order.
    /// </summary>
    private void BindGridView()
    {
        DateTime from = Conversion.TryCastDate(this.fromDate);
        DateTime to = Conversion.TryCastDate(this.toDate);

        this.statement = Data.Reports.AccountStatement.GetAccountStatement(this.catalog, from, to, this.userId,
            this.accountNumber, this.officeId);
    }

    /// <summary>
    ///     Port of CreateAccountOverviewPanel() + CreateTableBody(): the panel is CLEARED and
    ///     rebuilt, and a null view leaves it empty (the original returned before setting the
    ///     header literal).
    /// </summary>
    private void CreateAccountOverviewPanel()
    {
        this.overview = Data.Reports.AccountStatement.GetAccountOverview(this.catalog, this.accountNumber);
    }
}
